{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"exciting-arduous-borzoi","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe `_shadow` helper is md5-identical in `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py:52`, `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py:43`, `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:122` (6/34/24 call sites) with a fourth variant `src/rebar/_lib_ops.py:29` taking `(repo_root, surface)`; `_ticket_id` is AST-identical in `src/rebar/llm/workflow/steps.py:35` and `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/decide_ops.py:52`; `_positive_int` in `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/request.py:24` and `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/reconcile.py:18`. These are the token-identical twins the AST scan finds; RP-04 (`vibrant-legal-hind`) owns operation-scoped config composition and does not touch these helpers.\n\n## Approach\nOne `shadow(surface, repo_root=None)` in `src/rebar/_operation_config.py` (or the module `_lib_ops` already imports for the operation snapshot), imported by the four modules; `_ticket_id` moves to `src/rebar/llm/workflow/step_contracts.py`; `_positive_int` to `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/_common.py` (new). Guard: `tokensave`-style AST-isomorphism is not required — a test asserts each helper name is defined once under `src/rebar`.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/_operation_config.py`, `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py`, `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py`, `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py`, `src/rebar/_lib_ops.py`, `src/rebar/llm/workflow/steps.py`, `src/rebar/llm/workflow/step_contracts.py`, `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/decide_ops.py`, `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/request.py`, `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/reconcile.py`, `tests/unit/test_single_definition_helpers.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\nMechanical refactor; no new behaviour. Pinning: `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp.py`, `tests/unit/test_mcp_*`, the plan-review decide tests, and `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_request*.py` pass unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `def _shadow`, `def _ticket_id`, `def _positive_int` each occur once under `src/rebar`; checked by the new test.\n- [ ] All 64 `_shadow` call sites resolve through the import with no signature change; checked by `make typecheck` and the MCP facade tests.\n- [ ] Net non-test LOC is negative; checked by `git show --numstat`.\n","id":"7931-faee-53ba-47b1","parent_id":"2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a","priority":2,"tags":["consolidation","janitor","fortnight-review"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Single definitions for the token-identical helpers (_shadow, _ticket_id, _positive_int)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787352394860525001,"uuid":"3b664833-498e-419e-893c-171d660c953e"}